``peat pillage`` can now read EnCase/Expert Witness (EWF: ``.E01``, ``.Ex01``, ``.S01``) disk images with any number of segments, as well as raw, split raw (``.001``), VMDK (including VMware ESXi disks), VHD/VHDX and qcow2 images, without mounting them. This works on Windows, macOS and Linux without root, searches every partition (GPT or MBR) with an NTFS, FAT/exFAT or ext2/3/4 filesystem, and saves a ``pillage-summary.json`` summary of the image and the copied files. The new ``pillage_backend`` option (``--pillage-backend``) chooses between reading images directly (``library``), mounting them with ``qemu-nbd`` as before (``mount``), or ``auto`` (the default, which uses ``library`` when it supports the image). Images are treated as untrusted input: hard links are copied only once, and the new ``max_file_size`` and ``max_total_size`` Pillage options and a free disk space check limit how much is copied.
